<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Floating-overlay button styles (Spec 3 §3.2).

    Two narrow Material 3 button variants used exclusively by
    `overlay_5button_layout.xml`:

      - `OverlayButton.Primary` — the record/send button (text + leading
        icon). Filled `Widget.Material3.Button`; its static base is
        `colorPrimary`, but the render path overrides the container tint
        to the translucent third colour (see below), and the recording
        animation controller owns it while a recording is active.
      - `OverlayButton.Icon` — Pause / Trash / Close (icon-only, 48 dp
        square). Filled-tonal icon button ⇒ `colorSecondaryContainer`
        container (the third background colour, painted translucent by
        the render path — see below).

    Both inherit Material 3 defaults — no `cornerRadius` override so the
    buttons match the keyboard-surface buttons (record_btn / trash_btn /
    pause_btn / enter_btn — none of them sets cornerRadius either, so
    they all share the Material 3 pill-shape default). The previous 12dp
    override was removed 2026-05-22 per user-req "Buttons sollen genauso
    ausschauen wie auf der normalen Tastatur, also auch mit den gleichen
    Rundungen".

    # Widget-transparency: buttons follow the slider too (2026-07-03, revised)

    These styles only supply the STATIC baseline container colour used
    for tools-preview and the 100 %-opacity case. The *live* container
    fill is written per render tick by
    `OverlayBackend.applyBackgroundOpacity`, which paints EVERY overlay
    button with the overlay's third background colour
    (`colorSecondaryContainer`) at the current `Pref.WidgetOpacity`
    alpha — so the buttons dim together with the card (user request
    2026-07-03: "grundsätzlich alle Buttons im Widget-Modus … mit
    Opacity").

    Both variants therefore resolve to `colorSecondaryContainer` as the
    filled tint base: the icon buttons via
    `Widget.Material3.Button.IconButton.Filled.Tonal`. A static style
    cannot carry the dynamic slider alpha (a `MaterialButton`'s container
    fill is its `backgroundTintList`), so the alpha lives in the render
    path next to the card fill — see the single-source-of-truth policy in
    `OverlayCardFill` and the KDoc on `applyBackgroundOpacity`. Only the
    container fill is tinted; icons/text keep full opacity.

    (History: an earlier 2026-07-03 iteration deliberately kept the
    buttons opaque — that was reverted per the newer user request above;
    see `overlay-widget-transparency.md` §7 change history.)

    @see docs/plans/2026-05-07 - dictate-keyboard-layout-refactor/research/3-floating-overlay/3-floating-overlay.reviewed.md §3.2
    @see docs/research/2026-07-02 - overlay-widget-transparency.md §3.3
-->
<resources>

    <style name="OverlayButton.Primary" parent="Widget.Material3.Button">
        <item name="android:textAllCaps">false</item>
    </style>

    <!-- Filled-tonal ⇒ opaque colorSecondaryContainer container. Keeps
         the M3 icon-button sizing/ripple/pill-shape while guaranteeing
         the button box stays fully opaque over a translucent card. -->
    <style name="OverlayButton.Icon" parent="Widget.Material3.Button.IconButton.Filled.Tonal" />

</resources>
